From 967159043230783c5c77827876b0abced1185f8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:10:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent,kanban): [daveey] standing instructions survive
 compaction, reach workers, and hold don't-wait blocks

A relayed 'dont block, dont wait' was paraphrased by compaction into its opposite and the agent later
blocked on the user (self-heal agent-aa8d66631c).

- agent/standing_instructions.py: shared extractor for explicit 'standing: <words>' lines and
  don't-wait directives in real/relayed user messages.
- context compressor: every summary (lean and legacy) ends with a 'Standing instructions (still in
  force)' section, word for word; standing: lines are re-read from earlier summaries so they survive
  repeated compaction.
- build_worker_context: standing: lines from the body and ANY comment render up front (the comment
  thread is tail-capped).
- kanban_block: a needs_input/human_request block on a card with a standing don't-wait is held once
  with the words quoted back and a standing_wait_hold event; a second call lands it.
---
